// t_80dad2dd: a fragment program whose colour output is DECLARED half.
//
// The reference compiles this to a single `MOVH o[COLH], f[TEX0]` - the
// output register is H0, the instruction carries fp16 precision, and the
// container's outputFromH0 flag is set.  The general path compiles the same
// source to `MOVR o[COLR]` with the flag clear and says nothing about it.
// The declared type is the ONLY thing that decides this: the same body at
// fp32 arithmetic under the reference's fast-precision switch turns MOVH but
// keeps o[COLR] and the clear flag, so this is not a question of how the body
// is computed.
void main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0, out half4 o : COLOR)
{
    o = t;
}
